{"id":"word:hebrew:H3669","type":"word","title":"כְּנַעַנִי","subtitle":"H3669 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"a Kenaanite or inhabitant of Kenaan; by implication, a pedlar (the Canaanites standing for their neighbors the Ishmaelites, who conducted mercantile caravans)","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to כְּנַעַנִי (H3669) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-m.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 73 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"כְּנַעַנִי (Kᵉnaʻanîy) means a Kenaanite or inhabitant of Kenaan; by implication, a pedlar (the Canaanites standing for their neighbors the Ishmaelites, who conducted mercantile caravans) First listed occurrence: 1Chr 2 3."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"כְּנַעַנִי","transliteration":"Kᵉnaʻanîy","pronunciation":"ken-ah-an-ee'","strong":"H3669","lemmaId":"hebrew:H3669","partOfSpeech":"n-m","forms":["הַֽ/כְּנַעֲנִי֙","הַֽ/כְּנַעֲנִ֖י","הַֽ/כְּנַעֲנִ֔י","הַֽ/כְּנַעֲנִ֛י","וְ/הַֽ/כְּנַעֲנִ֔י"],"morphs":[["HTd/Ngmsa",47],["HC/Td/Ngmsa",12],["HRd/Ngmsa",6],["HTd/Ngfsa",3],["HNgmsa",2],["HNgmpa",2],["HTd/Ngmpa",1]]},"definitions":{"short":"a Kenaanite or inhabitant of Kenaan; by implication, a pedlar (the Canaanites standing for their neighbors the Ishmaelites, who conducted mercantile caravans)","usage":"Canaanite, merchant, trafficker.","full":"H3669. Kna 'aniy I. כְּנַעֲנִי adjective and name, of a people of I. כְּנַעַן ; — usually masculine singular (הַ)כְּנַעֲנִי Gen 38:2 ; Num 21:1 +; feminine singular הַכְּנַעֲנִית Gen 46:10 = Exod 6:15 ; 1Chr 2:3 masculine plural (הַ)כְּנַעֲנִים Obadiah 20; Neh 9:24 ; &#8212; 1. adjective כ ׳אִישׁ Gen 38:2 (J). 2 with article as substantive, a. of individual , ׳מֶלֶךְעֲֿרָדהַכּ Num 21:1 (J) and hence 33:40 (P or R); feminine הַכְּנַעֲנִיתּ Gen 46:10 = Exod 6:15 (P) הַכְּנַעֲנִית בַּתשֿׁוּעַ 1Chr 2:3 . b. usually collective (with article) of pre-Israel in-habitants of כְּנַעַן (q. v.) Gen 12:6 ; 24:3 , 37 ; 50:11 (all J), Num 21:3 (J), Josh 13:3 (D), Judg 1:1 , 3 , 9 , 10 , 17 , many of whom continued to live in the midst of Israel, 1:27 ; 1:28 ; 1:29 ; 1:29 ; 1:30 ; 1:32 ; 1:33 ; Josh 16:10 (twice in verse); 17:12-13 , 16 , 18 (all J E), 1Kin 9:16 ; plural only Obadiah 20, and הַכְּנַעֲנִים הָאָרֶץ ישְׁבֵי Neh 9:24 ; הַכּ ׳מִשְׁמְּחוֺת Gen 10:18 , הַכּ ׳גְּבוּל 10:19 (both J), הַכּ ׳אֶרֶץ Exod 13:11 (JE), Ezek 16:3 ; often of part of the inhabitants, ׳הַכּ הָאָרֶץ ישְׁבֵי וְכָל Josh 7:9 (JE), Deut 11:30 ; with other proper name, of a people, + הַמְּרִזִּי Gen 13:7 ; 34:30 (both J), Judg 1:4-5 , + הָאֱמֹרִי Deut 1:7 ; Josh 5:1 ; 13:4 (all D); + הַחִוִּי 2Sam 24:7 ; + (יׅ עֲמָלֵקִ Num 14:25 , 43 , 45 ; especially in the list of peoples dispossessed by Israel, Gen 15:21 ; Exod 3:8 , 17 ; 13:5 ; 23:23 , 28 ; 33:2 ; 34:11 ; Num 13:29 ( ׳הַכּ dwelling by the sea and along Jordan [compare Deut 1:7 ; 11:30 ; Josh 5:1 ; 11:3 ; 13:4 ]; all these J E), Deut 7:1 ; 20:17 ; Josh 3:10 ; 9:1 ; 11:3 ; 12:8 ; 24:11 (all J E D), Judg 3:3 , 5 ; hence Ezra 9:1 ; Neh 9:8 . compare Dr Dt. p. 11, 13 f., 97, 133 . II. כְּנַעֲנִי noun masculine trader, merchant (compare II. כְּנַעַן ); only singular (but see below): — י כ׳בְּבֵית יִהְיֶה ׳וְלֹא עוֺד Zech 14:21 (probably); לַכּ נָָֽתְנָה ׳וַחֲגוֺר Prov 31:24 (|| וַתִּמְכֹּר עָֽשְׂתָה סָדִין ). **plural suffix כִּנְעָנֶיהָ (si vera lectio) Isa 23:8 (|| סֹחֲרֶיהָ ). In Zech 11:7 , 11 read perhaps (לִ)כְנַעֲנִיֵּי for ᵐ5 עֲנִיֵּי, (לָ)כֵן Ξαναναῖοι , Ξαναανῖτιν , Sta ZAW, 1881. 26 (who compare as to sense Hosea 12:8 ), compare Klo We Marti.","rootNote":"patrial from 3667 ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 2 3","keyReferences":["1Chr 2 3","1Kgs 9 16","2Sam 24 7","Deut 1 7","Deut 7 1","Deut 11 30","Deut 20 17","Exod 3 8"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":73,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Chr 2 3","book":"1Chr",